OpenMC 0.15.3 on Windows, patch 3 of 4: MSVC language and OpenMP fixes.
Taken from PR 2919, minus the files already in patch 2.
- shared_array.h: MSVC's OpenMP does not accept seq_cst on 'omp atomic' (per PR 2919).
- random_ray: PR 2919 reduces into a local instead of a class member ("must use temporary
  accumulator variable for OpenMP on Windows").
- event.h needs <tuple>; geometry.h forward-declares BoundaryInfo as class but it is a struct.
- 'and' alternative token in source.cpp (MSVC without /permissive-).
- M_PI is not defined by MSVC without _USE_MATH_DEFINES: use openmc PI (quartic_solver, plot.cpp).
- cell.cpp: the loop kept using an iterator after std::vector::erase invalidated it (undefined
  behaviour on every compiler; PR 2919 assigns the iterator returned by erase).
- secondary_correlated.cpp: initialise c_k1 (used-uninitialised diagnostic).

